{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_018Ceqg5iFEfkmWwWbsrEphK","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The file has been written. Here's a summary of what's in it:\n\n---\n\n## `/06-error-handling-resilience.md` — What's covered\n\n**7 Core Questions:**\n\n1. **Error taxonomy** — 6 categories (validation, network, card decline, authentication, fraud, rate limit), each with a different recoverability model and UX strategy. Includes a `classifyStripeError()` TypeScript function with explicit allowlist/denylist logic.\n\n2. **Decline codes & messaging** — Full `SPECIFIC_DECLINE_MESSAGES` / `SILENT_DECLINE_CODES` pattern in TypeScript. Explains *why* `stolen_card` gets the same generic message as `do_not_honor` (anti-card-testing), with a React `PaymentErrorAlert` component.\n\n3. **3DS authentication** — State machine for all failure modes (cancel, timeout, bank down), sequence diagram, and the critical `retrievePaymentIntent` pattern for resuming interrupted challenges across page reloads.\n\n4. **Network timeout vs. definitive failure** — The ambiguous-charge problem, idempotency key persistence strategy, and a flowchart for the PI status → recovery path decision tree.\n\n5. **Stripe.js load failure** — Timeout-wrapped `loadStripe()`, explicit fallback UI, what to log, and why self-hosting is a PCI violation.\n\n6. **Circuit breaker pattern** — Full TypeScript `CircuitBreaker` class (closed/open/half-open states), `sessionStorage` persistence across refreshes, and a state diagram.\n\n7. **Last-step server error UX** — Keeping Stripe Elements mounted across errors, the critical \"your card has not been charged\" copy, aria-live region, and why auto-retry is dangerous here.\n\n**3 Deep Questions:**\n\n8. **Full 3DS2 architecture** — Device fingerprinting phase, iframe vs. redirect challenge modes, serializing state to `sessionStorage` before redirect, recovering at `return_url` with `retrievePaymentIntent`, and a detailed sequence diagram for both paths.\n\n9. **Offline resilience** — `navigator.onLine` + Network Information API, idempotency-key-first queuing, retry-on-`online` event pattern, and — critically — an explicit enumeration of the limits of what the frontend can guarantee (Service Worker can't handle 3DS, `navigator.onLine` lies, PIs expire).\n\n10. **Debugging cross-origin Stripe iframe exceptions** — What Sentry can/cannot see across the Same-Origin Policy boundary, instrumentation strategy around (not inside) the iframe, segmentation analytics to find correlations, and mitigations including the `retrievePaymentIntent` safety check before showing any error to prevent \"failed\" messages on successful charges."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acb5585abdcd52dcd (use SendMessage with to: 'acb5585abdcd52dcd' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 36803\ntool_uses: 2\nduration_ms: 272870</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01PHe8LRAJRBSGkBNJq3XRRu","session_id":"9078f7bd-c9da-4434-af6f-ab88627aea1a","uuid":"d46a624f-ba0f-475e-8cf8-a1c4512cb057","timestamp":"2026-06-20T19:19:37.225Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write answers/06-error-handling-resilience.md for payments-system"}
